Non-ASCII text in strings and comments: accented Latin, CJK, emoji (an
astral-plane character, two UTF-16 code units) and a combining accent.
Diagnostic columns after non-ASCII text on the same line must stay
correct: the undeclared sMissing after an emoji on line 7 sits at column
17, counted in code points as the CLI contract specifies (A2), the emoji
being one character, and formatting must not mangle bytes.
-- input.ssl --
/* Résumé des échantillons — 样品摘要 🧪;
:DECLARE sGreeting, sLabel, sUnused;
sGreeting := "Grüße aus Zürich 👋";
sLabel := "試料番号: " + sGreeting + " café";
/* naïve — combining: é → é;
sLabel := sLabel + "🧪🧫";   :RETURN sLabel;
sLabel := "🧪" + sMissing;
-- format --
/* Résumé des échantillons — 样品摘要 🧪;
:DECLARE sGreeting, sLabel, sUnused;
sGreeting := "Grüße aus Zürich 👋";
sLabel := "試料番号: " + sGreeting + " café";
/* naïve — combining: é → é;
sLabel := sLabel + "🧪🧫";
:RETURN sLabel;
sLabel := "🧪" + sMissing;
